Of course some other names could be jokes in Spanish or Russian...
>>
>> Or Arabic, or Japanese, or Jewish, or Afrikaans....


  Just to threadjack here... There is no language called "Jewish" in
English.  (Although the word "Yiddish" does mean "Jewish" in Yiddish).
 Jewish is the adjectival form of Jew, someone of that
religion/ethnicity/culture (like me {;-)>  ).  There are many specifically
"Jewish" languages -- Hebrew (about half dozen varieties evolved over the
millennia), Yiddish (spoken by the Jews in Eastern and Central Europe),
Ladino (spoken by the Jews in the Iberian peninsula), etc. But Jews can and
do  (usually)  speak the majority language of whatever land they find
themselves in.

   As for the project itself -- ah, well.  Guess that leaves me out of this
new incarnation.  I'm no graphic artist.

                         --gejyspa

